{
  "name": "@wenathlan/saddle-web",
  "version": "2.1.5",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "description": "saddle web console (the merged e2ugh sandbox surface): the universal tsx interface plus the self-hosted zero-dependency node api (web/server.ts) and the platform deploy adapters (vercel.json, netlify.toml) at the deploy root; static-first, no serverless functions",
  "_comment": "the web manifest: the deploy root owns its package. the dependency set mirrors the repository-root package.json one-to-one (every package at the root lives here and every package here lives at the root - the same set, kept in lockstep) so the vite build runs standalone (cd web && npm install && npm run build) and the vercel/netlify deploy roots resolve their toolchain. this package is NEVER published to npm, github packages or any registry - the published package is the central @wenathlan/saddle (repository root) which ships the engine without web/. the start script exists only for self-hosted nodes (docker, vps, caddy) where web/server.ts serves the built dist/public and the /api/v1 contract. the interface sources are tsx/ts only (the 2.1.4 typescript conversion): designs in tsx, logic in ts, zero js at the web root.",
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=26.7.0"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.ts",
    "dev": "vite --host",
    "build": "vite build",
    "check": "tsc --noEmit",
    "serve": "node server.ts"
  },
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
